From 95a22117deff30215137613f1bdd63c10056d2fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PhialsBasement <155454343+PhialsBasement@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 03:01:14 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] GPU profiling and terrain support: draw times, section
 cycles, rigid motion vectors

- Per-draw GPU timestamps naming the owner node, pass, surface and
  instance (GODOT_DRAW_TIMES), with a 1x1-scissor geometry replay
  (GODOT_DRAW_GEO); debug/settings/profiler/split_instances turns
  instancing off.
- Section profiler (GODOT_SECTION_PROFILE=frames): profile_clock()
  and profile_add() in shaders and engine stage markers read the
  subgroup clock (VK_KHR_shader_clock) into per-draw counters,
  printed as SECT| lines; GODOT_SECTION_ONLY=n compiles one section
  in. Compiled out when unset.
- IN_DEPTH_PREPASS shader built-in.
- motion_vectors_rigid render mode: last frame's position from this
  frame's model-space vertex, vertex() runs once under TAA.
- re-spirv accepts OpReadClockKHR.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
